      sections: [{"id":"s1","title":"Case Studies","whyItMatters":"Apply Excel to real business problems.","content":"**Case Study 1: Retail Analytics**\n\nA retail chain needs to analyze 50 stores' performance. Build a dashboard showing revenue, foot traffic, conversion rate, and inventory turnover.\n\n**Case Study 2: Financial Planning**\n\nA startup needs a 3-year financial model with revenue projections, expense budgets, and cash flow forecasts.\n\n**Case Study 3: Operations Optimization**\n\nA warehouse needs to optimize inventory levels. Build an inventory analysis system with reorder points and EOQ calculations.\n\n**Case Study 4: HR Analytics**\n\nA growing company needs to analyze hiring data, turnover trends, and department growth patterns.\n\n```text\nCase Study Dashboard:\n====================\n\nStore Performance:\n  Revenue: =SUM(Sales[Amount])\n  Conversion: =Orders/Visitors\n  YoY Growth: =(ThisYear-LastYear)/LastYear\n\nFinancial Model:\n  Revenue Growth: 20% YoY\n  Gross Margin: 65%\n  Operating Expenses: 40%\n  Net Income: 15%\n```\n\nSolve real business problems with Excel.","codeExamples":[{"id":"s1","title":"Case Study","description":"Analyze a business case","code":{"excel":"Case Study Analysis\n===================\n\nRevenue Analysis:\n=SUMIF(Stores[Region],\"West\",Sales[Amount])\n\nGrowth Rate:\n=(Current-Previous)/Previous\n\nForecast:\n=FORECAST(Month,Revenue,Months)"},"explanation":"Apply Excel to real business cases."}]}],
